<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Online Inference<span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">.</span></span>
The fine-tuned models are deployed for online inference without further updates to the model parameters or router.
The inference results are presented in Fig. <a href="#S5.F3" title="Fig. 3 ‣ V-B Results with Fine-tuning and Inference ‣ V Performance Evaluation ‣ Faster, Smaller, and Smarter: Task-Aware Expert Merging for Online MoE Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, including the average performance across tasks (detailed per-task metrics are provided in Tab. <a href="#S5.T2" title="TABLE II ‣ V-B Results with Fine-tuning and Inference ‣ V Performance Evaluation ‣ Faster, Smaller, and Smarter: Task-Aware Expert Merging for Online MoE Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">II</span></a>), inference time per batch, and memory usage.
We highlight three main observations:
<span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">First</span>, <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span> achieves the <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">best average performance</span> along with consistently better performance on individual tasks.
This is because it dynamically adjusts the expert merging strategy based on online task features and fully exploits the information from multiple experts.
<span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Second</span>, <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span> demonstrates highly <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">efficient inference speed</span>, requiring only one expert merging decision and execution at the start of each time slot. This reduces inference time per batch by <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="65\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">65</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">65\%</annotation></semantics></math> compared to <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RL</span> and <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Switch</span>, nearly <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="99\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">99</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">99\%</annotation></semantics></math> over <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Smear</span>.
<span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Third</span>, <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span> achieves the <span id="S5.SS2.p2.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">lowest memory consumption</span>. Since only the merged model is loaded,
it reduces memory use by <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">20</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20\%</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="25\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">25</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">25\%</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">V-C</span> </span><span id="S5.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Results with Online Learning for Inference</span></h3>

<figure id="S5.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<table id="S5.F4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S5.F4.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.F4.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">

<div id="S5.F4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:172.5pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.19781v1/reward_time.svg" id="S5.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:226/183;" width="226" height="183"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering">(a) Online Reward</figcaption>
</div>
<div id="S5.F4.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:172.5pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.19781v1/bert_metric.svg" id="S5.F4.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/183;" width="238" height="183"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering">(b) Average Accuracy</figcaption>
</div></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 4: </span>Online Inference with BERT-based MoE.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here, we focus on BERT-based MoE models that do not require fine-tuning and allow the router to be trained online during inference. Since loss information is unavailable during online inference, traditional router training methods cannot be applied. Thus, we compare our <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span> with model merging methods.
The online learning performance is shown in Fig. <a href="#S5.F4" title="Fig. 4 ‣ V-C Results with Online Learning for Inference ‣ V Performance Evaluation ‣ Faster, Smaller, and Smarter: Task-Aware Expert Merging for Online MoE Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>(a). Although <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span> performs worse in the early stages due to the limited number of candidate merging weights, it converges faster and achieves better performance than <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Nucb</span> as the partition tree becomes more refined over time.
This result highlights the advantage of our tree partitioning strategy, which efficiently explores the search space during online updates.
Overall, <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span> demonstrates strong online learning capability.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<table id="S5.F6.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S5.F6.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.F6.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">

<div id="S5.F6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:165.6pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.19781v1/bert_dynamic.svg" id="S5.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:217/171;" width="217" height="171"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_block">Fig. 5: </span>Online inference per slot performance with BERT-based MoE.</figcaption>
</div>
<div id="S5.F6.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:165.6pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.19781v1/router_cost.svg" id="S5.F6.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:229/175;" width="229" height="175"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_block">Fig. 6: </span>Update and routing overhead of <span id="S5.F6.2.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span> under different system scales.</figcaption>
</div></td></tr>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">After <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn mathsize="0.900em">5000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5000</annotation></semantics></math> time slots of online learning, we further evaluate the performance over additional time slots. The results under both fixed and dynamic task features are shown in Fig. <a href="#S5.F4" title="Fig. 4 ‣ V-C Results with Online Learning for Inference ‣ V Performance Evaluation ‣ Faster, Smaller, and Smarter: Task-Aware Expert Merging for Online MoE Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>(b) and the per-slot performance details under dynamic task features are shown in Fig. <a href="#S5.F6" title="Fig. 6 ‣ V-C Results with Online Learning for Inference ‣ V Performance Evaluation ‣ Faster, Smaller, and Smarter: Task-Aware Expert Merging for Online MoE Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.
We can observe that <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span>
outperforms the baselines by up to <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">9</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9\%</annotation></semantics></math> under fixed task features and by <math id="S5.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5-10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">5</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5-10\%</annotation></semantics></math> under dynamic task features.
The performance gain is especially notable in dynamic settings, as <span id="S5.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span> adapts to evolving task distributions in real-time by merging experts based on task features. This adaptability enables it to surpass other methods that rely on static or less flexible merging strategies.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS4.6" class="ltx_text">V-D</span> </span><span id="S5.SS4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Scalability and Ablation study</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Scalability Evaluation<span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">.</span></span> To evaluate the scalability of <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span>, we conduct experiments on MoE models with 4 to 192 experts. Fig. <a href="#S5.F6" title="Fig. 6 ‣ V-C Results with Online Learning for Inference ‣ V Performance Evaluation ‣ Faster, Smaller, and Smarter: Task-Aware Expert Merging for Online MoE Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows the number of update steps required to identify 20 feasible leaf nodes and the time needed to compute the optimal merging weight from them. The results show that as the number of experts increases, more update steps are required due to the higher dimensionality of the decision space <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, which leads to more partitioning options. Although the routing time per decision also increases with the number of experts, it remains low (less than 0.4 ms even when <math id="S5.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=192" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">K</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">192</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=192</annotation></semantics></math>). These results indicate that <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span> maintains high efficiency and scalability in large-scale settings.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<table id="S5.F7.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="S5.F7.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.F7.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">

<div id="S5.F7.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:172.5pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.19781v1/figure_rho.svg" id="S5.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/183;" width="238" height="183"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering">(a) Smoothness Parameter <math id="S5.F7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</div>
<div id="S5.F7.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_block ltx_minipage ltx_align_top" style="width:172.5pt;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.19781v1/figure_lr.svg" id="S5.F7.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/183;" width="238" height="183"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering">(b) Learning Rate <math id="S5.F7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</div></td></tr>
</table>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 7: </span>Learning performance of <span id="S5.F7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span> with T5-based MoE under different settings of parameters.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Ablation Study<span id="S5.SS4.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">.</span></span> We analyze the sensitivity of our <span id="S5.SS4.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span> to key hyperparameters.
Fig. <a href="#S5.F7" title="Fig. 7 ‣ V-D Scalability and Ablation study ‣ V Performance Evaluation ‣ Faster, Smaller, and Smarter: Task-Aware Expert Merging for Online MoE Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> presents the learning performance of the T5-based MoE under different settings of the smoothness parameter <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> and the neural network learning rate <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>.
A smaller <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> makes <span id="S5.SS4.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span> more conservative when partitioning the cover tree, requiring more observations before a node is expanded.
As seen in Fig. <a href="#S5.F7" title="Fig. 7 ‣ V-D Scalability and Ablation study ‣ V Performance Evaluation ‣ Faster, Smaller, and Smarter: Task-Aware Expert Merging for Online MoE Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, a smaller <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> shortens the initial random phase, since the merging weights exhibit less variation and allow faster fine-tuning. However, this leads to relatively lower final performance, as the decision space is insufficiently explored. In contrast, a larger <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> allows for better exploration of the decision space but results in longer initial random times and slower fine-tuning. Therefore, choosing an appropriate value of <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is critical for balancing exploration and exploitation.
The learning rate <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> controls the magnitude of updates during the training of the neural network. A higher learning rate accelerates convergence but may cause instability, while a lower learning rate results in more stable training but slower progress. Tuning <math id="S5.SS4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> is essential to achieve both stability and efficient convergence.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">VI </span><span id="S6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Conclusion</span></h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we propose <span id="S6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span>, a tree-structured adaptive neural bandit router, to improve the efficiency of online inference with MoEs.
By utilizing task distributions, which are easily obtained in online environments,
<span id="S6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span> dynamically merges experts within a given pre-trained MoE in a task-aware manner, enabling a single merged expert to handle multiple tasks.
This is achieved through a tree-structured partitioning method that efficiently explores the continuous decision space, followed by a neural bandit approach that models the non-linear mapping between merging weights and performance rewards, and selects the optimal merging weight. Through both theoretical analysis and extensive experiments, we show that <span id="S6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span> achieves sublinear regret and significantly reduces memory usage and inference latency while maintaining a high accuracy.
These advantages make <span id="S6.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span> particularly suitable for deploying MoE models in resource-constrained settings, such as edge networks.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To reduce interference among multiple experts <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>, <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>, future work could explore grouping similar experts for merging. This can be achieved by applying advanced clustering techniques <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">51</a>]</cite> to dynamically form expert groups, which could improve both efficiency and accuracy across various applications.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Appendix</h2>

<section id="Sx1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="Sx1.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">VI-A</span> </span><span id="Sx1.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Lemma 1</span></h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Besides the assumptions in Sec. <a href="#S4.SS4" title="IV-D Theoretical Analysis ‣ IV Algorithm Design ‣ Faster, Smaller, and Smarter: Task-Aware Expert Merging for Online MoE Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">IV-D</span></a>, we also have the following assumption.</p>
</div>
<div id="ThmAssumption3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_Assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="ThmAssumption3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 3</span></span><span id="ThmAssumption3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="ThmAssumption3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="ThmAssumption3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="ThmAssumption3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(Near-Optimality dimension)</span><span id="ThmAssumption3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
Let <math id="ThmAssumption3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=3\nu_{1}\rho^{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=3\nu_{1}\rho^{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="ThmAssumption3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{\prime}=\nu_{2}\rho^{h}&lt;\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi></msup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">&lt;</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\prime}=\nu_{2}\rho^{h}&lt;\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. For any subset of <math id="ThmAssumption3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-optimal nodes <math id="ThmAssumption3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{\epsilon}=\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}:f^{*}-f(\boldsymbol{x})\leq\epsilon\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐱</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐱</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{\epsilon}=\{\boldsymbol{x}\in\mathcal{X}:f^{*}-f(\boldsymbol{x})\leq\epsilon\}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a constant <math id="ThmAssumption3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="ThmAssumption3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\mathcal{X}_{\epsilon},\ell,\epsilon^{\prime})\leq C(\epsilon^{\prime})^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\mathcal{X}_{\epsilon},\ell,\epsilon^{\prime})\leq C(\epsilon^{\prime})^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="ThmAssumption3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> is the near-optimality dimension of <math id="ThmAssumption3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="ThmAssumption3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(\mathcal{X}_{\epsilon},\ell,\epsilon^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(\mathcal{X}_{\epsilon},\ell,\epsilon^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="ThmAssumption3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>-cover number of <math id="ThmAssumption3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the dissimilarity measure <math id="ThmAssumption3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Then, we characterize the complexity of the problem using the near-optimality dimension. We first establish an upper bound on the maximum depth of the partition tree in <span id="Sx1.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Tanbr</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="ThmLemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_Lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="ThmLemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="ThmLemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="ThmLemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="ThmLemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="ThmLemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given the threshold <math id="ThmLemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{h}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{h}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> defined in Eq. (<a href="#S4.E2" title="In IV-B Tree-Structured Measurable Space Partitioning ‣ IV Algorithm Design ‣ Faster, Smaller, and Smarter: Task-Aware Expert Merging for Online MoE Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), the depth <math id="ThmLemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(t)</annotation></semantics></math> of the tree <math id="ThmLemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℋ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by:</span></p>
<table id="Sx1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(t)\leq H_{max}(T)\leq\frac{1}{1-\rho}\log\frac{T\nu_{1}^{2}}{C^{2}\log(T/\delta)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">H</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">x</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(t)\leq H_{max}(T)\leq\frac{1}{1-\rho}\log\frac{T\nu_{1}^{2}}{C^{2}\log(T/\delta)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Proof<span id="Sx1.SS1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">.</span></span>
Recall that a node <math id="Sx1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h,i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h,i)</annotation></semantics></math> is expanded only when its pull count <math id="Sx1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{h,i}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">P</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{h,i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> exceeds the threshold <math id="Sx1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{h}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{h}(t)</annotation></semantics></math>. To find the maximum possible depth <math id="Sx1.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(t)</annotation></semantics></math> of any node that may be expanded up to round <math id="Sx1.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider the condition under which a node can be expanded: <math id="Sx1.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{h}(t)\leq t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{h}(t)\leq t</annotation></semantics></math>. By substituting the expression for <math id="Sx1.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{h}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">τ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{h}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> from Eq. (<a href="#S4.E2" title="In IV-B Tree-Structured Measurable Space Partitioning ‣ IV Algorithm Design ‣ Faster, Smaller, and Smarter: Task-Aware Expert Merging for Online MoE Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>), we obtain:
<math id="Sx1.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{C^{2}\log(t/\delta)}{\nu_{1}^{2}}\rho^{-2h}\leq t\Rightarrow\rho^{-2h}\leq\frac{t\nu_{1}^{2}}{C^{2}\log(t/\delta)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{C^{2}\log(t/\delta)}{\nu_{1}^{2}}\rho^{-2h}\leq t\Rightarrow\rho^{-2h}\leq\frac{t\nu_{1}^{2}}{C^{2}\log(t/\delta)}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Taking the logarithm on both sides, we have the depth <math id="Sx1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(t)</annotation></semantics></math> bounded by:
<math id="Sx1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(t)\leq\frac{1}{2\log(1/\rho)}\log\left(\frac{t\nu_{1}^{2}}{C^{2}\log(t/\delta)}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(t)\leq\frac{1}{2\log(1/\rho)}\log\left(\frac{t\nu_{1}^{2}}{C^{2}\log(t/\delta)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math>
To simplify the upper bound to depend solely on <math id="Sx1.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the inequalities <math id="Sx1.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Sx1.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(t/\delta)\geq\log(T/\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≥</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(t/\delta)\geq\log(T/\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>. This gives:</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Sx1.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle H(T)\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle H(T)\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{2\log(1/\rho)}\log(\frac{T\nu_{1}^{2}}{C^{2}\log(T/\delta)})\leq\frac{1}{1-\rho}\log(\frac{T\nu_{1}^{2}}{C^{2}\log(T/\delta)})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{2\log(1/\rho)}\log(\frac{T\nu_{1}^{2}}{C^{2}\log(T/\delta)})\leq\frac{1}{1-\rho}\log(\frac{T\nu_{1}^{2}}{C^{2}\log(T/\delta)}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">where the second inequality follows <math id="Sx1.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\log(1/\rho)\geq 1-\rho,\forall\rho\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≥</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\log(1/\rho)\geq 1-\rho,\forall\rho\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. This completes the proof of Lemma <a href="#ThmLemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ VI-A Proof of Lemma 1 ‣ Appendix ‣ Faster, Smaller, and Smarter: Task-Aware Expert Merging for Online MoE Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Lemma <a href="#ThmLemma2" title="Lemma 2. ‣ VI-A Proof of Lemma 1 ‣ Appendix ‣ Faster, Smaller, and Smarter: Task-Aware Expert Merging for Online MoE Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> ensures that the maximum depth of the tree does not exceed <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\log T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\log T)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Furthermore, we derive an upper bound on the number of arms at any time slot, denoted by <math id="Sx1.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> as:</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Sx1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Sx1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{t}\leq\frac{2^{1/(1-\rho)}t\nu_{1}^{2}}{C^{2}\log(T/\delta)}\leq\frac{2^{1/(1-\rho)}T\nu_{1}^{2}}{C^{2}\log(T/\delta)}=N." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{t}\leq\frac{2^{1/(1-\rho)}t\nu_{1}^{2}}{C^{2}\log(T/\delta)}\leq\frac{2^{1/(1-\rho)}T\nu_{1}^{2}}{C^{2}\log(T/\delta)}=N.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="Sx1.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">VI-B</span> </span><span id="Sx1.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Theorem 1</span></h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we show the definition of the Neural Tangent Kernel (NTK) matrix and its effective dimension.</p>
</div>
<div id="ThmDefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_Definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="ThmDefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="ThmDefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="ThmDefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="ThmDefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="ThmDefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="ThmDefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐌</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{M}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the NTK matrix associated with <math id="ThmDefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒳</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>. The effective dimension <math id="ThmDefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{d}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="ThmDefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐌</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, with regularization parameter <math id="ThmDefinition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, is defined by: <math id="ThmDefinition1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{d}=\frac{\log\det(\boldsymbol{I}+\boldsymbol{M}/\lambda)}{\log(1+TN/\lambda)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">det</mo><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐈</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐌</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{d}=\frac{\log\det(\boldsymbol{I}+\boldsymbol{M}/\lambda)}{\log(1+TN/\lambda)}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The NTK matrix <math id="Sx1.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝑴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{M}</annotation></semantics></math> is constructed recursively, layer by layer, from the input to the output of the neural network <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">52</a>]</cite>. The effective dimension <math id="Sx1.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{d}</annotation></semantics></math> captures the intrinsic dimensionality of the input in the Reproducing Kernel Hilbert Space (RKHS) induced by the NTK. For additional details, we refer the reader to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="ThmLemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_Lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="ThmLemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="ThmLemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="ThmLemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="ThmLemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">(Lemma 5.2 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>)<span id="ThmLemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
There exist positive constants <math id="ThmLemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{C}_{1},\bar{C}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{C}_{1},\bar{C}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="ThmLemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="ThmLemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\leq\bar{C}_{1}(TwL+w\lambda)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">η</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\leq\bar{C}_{1}(TwL+w\lambda)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="ThmLemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\geq\bar{C}_{2}\max\left\{T^{7}\lambda^{-7}L^{21}(\log w)^{3},\lambda^{-\frac{1}{2}}L^{-\frac{3}{2}}(\log(TNL^{2}/\delta))^{\frac{3}{2}}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">max</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">7</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">7</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">21</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn></msup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\geq\bar{C}_{2}\max\left\{T^{7}\lambda^{-7}L^{21}(\log w)^{3},\lambda^{-\frac{1}{2}}L^{-\frac{3}{2}}(\log(TNL^{2}/\delta))^{\frac{3}{2}}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math>,
then with probability at least <math id="ThmLemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have: <math id="ThmLemma3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}\|_{2}\leq 2\sqrt{t/(w\lambda)},\|\boldsymbol{\xi}^{*}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t}\|_{\boldsymbol{Z}_{t}}\leq\gamma_{t}/\sqrt{w},\forall t\in\mathcal{T}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝛏</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝛏</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝛏</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝛏</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐙</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">γ</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><msqrt><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒯</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}\|_{2}\leq 2\sqrt{t/(w\lambda)},\|\boldsymbol{\xi}^{*}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t}\|_{\boldsymbol{Z}_{t}}\leq\gamma_{t}/\sqrt{w},\forall t\in\mathcal{T}.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="ThmLemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_Lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="ThmLemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="ThmLemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="ThmLemma4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="ThmLemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="ThmLemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="ThmLemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h_{t}^{*},i_{t}^{*})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h_{t}^{*},i_{t}^{*})</annotation></semantics></math> be the leaf node that contains <math id="ThmLemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{x}_{t}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{x}_{t}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>.
There exist positive constants <math id="ThmLemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{C}_{1},\overline{C}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{C}_{1},\overline{C}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="ThmLemma4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="ThmLemma4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="ThmLemma4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy the same conditions as in Lemma <a href="#ThmLemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ VI-B Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ Appendix ‣ Faster, Smaller, and Smarter: Task-Aware Expert Merging for Online MoE Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, then with probability at least <math id="ThmLemma4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\small f_{1}^{*}(\boldsymbol{x}_{t}^{*})-f_{1}^{*}(\boldsymbol{x}_{h_{t},i_{t}})\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\small f_{1}^{*}(\boldsymbol{x}_{t}^{*})-f_{1}^{*}(\boldsymbol{x}_{h_{t},i_{t}})\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle 2\min\{\gamma_{t-1}\|\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x}_{h_{t},i_{t}},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1})/\sqrt{w}\|_{\boldsymbol{Z}_{t-1}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>min</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒈</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝝃</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>w</mi></msqrt><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝒁</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\min\{\gamma_{t-1}\|\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x}_{h_{t},i_{t}},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1})/\sqrt{w}\|_{\boldsymbol{Z}_{t-1}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.E9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle 1\}+2\bar{\Gamma}+\nu_{1}\rho^{h_{t}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1\}+2\bar{\Gamma}+\nu_{1}\rho^{h_{t}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="ThmLemma4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="ThmLemma4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="ThmLemma4.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bar{\Gamma}=\overline{C}_{1}w^{-1/6}\sqrt{\log w}t^{2/3}\lambda^{-2/3}L^{3}+\overline{C}_{2}(\sqrt{2\boldsymbol{m}^{\top}\boldsymbol{M}^{-1}\boldsymbol{m}}+2\sqrt{t/\lambda})w^{-1/6}\sqrt{\log w}t^{1/6}\lambda^{-1/6}L^{7/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">6</mn></mrow></msup><msqrt><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi></mrow></msqrt><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐦</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐌</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝐦</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">6</mn></mrow></msup><msqrt><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi></mrow></msqrt><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">6</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">6</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">7</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\Gamma}=\overline{C}_{1}w^{-1/6}\sqrt{\log w}t^{2/3}\lambda^{-2/3}L^{3}+\overline{C}_{2}(\sqrt{2\boldsymbol{m}^{\top}\boldsymbol{M}^{-1}\boldsymbol{m}}+2\sqrt{t/\lambda})w^{-1/6}\sqrt{\log w}t^{1/6}\lambda^{-1/6}L^{7/2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We now prove that the cumulative regret satisfies:</p>
<table id="Sx1.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.E10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle R_{T}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">R</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle R_{T}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.E10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\left[f_{1}^{*}(\boldsymbol{x}_{t}^{*})-f_{1}^{*}(\boldsymbol{x}_{h_{t},i_{t}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\left[f_{1}^{*}(\boldsymbol{x}_{t}^{*})-f_{1}^{*}(\boldsymbol{x}_{h_{t},i_{t}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\sqrt{T\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\min\{\gamma_{t-1}^{2}\|\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x}_{h_{t},i_{t}},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1})/\sqrt{w}\|_{\boldsymbol{Z}_{t-1}}^{2},1\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathsize="0.900em">γ</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒈</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">i</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><msqrt><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒁</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\sqrt{T\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\min\{\gamma_{t-1}^{2}\|\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x}_{h_{t},i_{t}},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1})/\sqrt{w}\|_{\boldsymbol{Z}_{t-1}}^{2},1\}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+2T\bar{\Gamma}+\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\nu_{1}\rho^{h_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em" mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" movablelimits="false" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">ν</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">ρ</mi><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">h</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+2T\bar{\Gamma}+\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\nu_{1}\rho^{h_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle 3\sqrt{T}\sqrt{\tilde{d}\log(1+TN/\lambda)+2}\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn><msqrt><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi></msqrt><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em">⋅</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 3\sqrt{T}\sqrt{\tilde{d}\log(1+TN/\lambda)+2}\cdot</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\upsilon\sqrt{\tilde{d}\log(1+TN/\lambda)+2-2\log\delta}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">υ</mi><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">d</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">N</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[\upsilon\sqrt{\tilde{d}\log(1+TN/\lambda)+2-2\log\delta}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left.+(\lambda+C_{3}TL)(1-\eta w\lambda)^{1/2}\sqrt{T/\lambda}+2\sqrt{\lambda S}\right]+T+1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn></msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">η</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></mrow></msup><msqrt><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><msqrt><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">S</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>]</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">T</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">+</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.+(\lambda+C_{3}TL)(1-\eta w\lambda)^{1/2}\sqrt{T/\lambda}+2\sqrt{\lambda S}\right]+T+1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where the first inequality follows from Lemma <a href="#ThmLemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ VI-B Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ Appendix ‣ Faster, Smaller, and Smarter: Task-Aware Expert Merging for Online MoE Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> and the Cauchy–Schwarz inequality; the second inequality follows by applying Lemma 5.4 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">28</a>]</cite>, valid for sufficiently large <math id="Sx1.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math>. This completes the proof of Theorem <a href="#ThmTheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ IV-D Theoretical Analysis ‣ IV Algorithm Design ‣ Faster, Smaller, and Smarter: Task-Aware Expert Merging for Online MoE Inference" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="Sx1.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">VI-C</span> </span><span id="Sx1.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof of Lemma 4</span></h3>

<div id="Sx1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the difference between the estimated value and the real value, we have:</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Sx1.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.E11.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\|f(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1})-&lt;\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}),\boldsymbol{\xi}^{*}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}&gt;\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">&lt;</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒈</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|f(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1})-&lt;\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}),\boldsymbol{\xi}^{*}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}&gt;\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="0.900em">=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\|f(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1})-f(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0})-&lt;\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}),\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">&lt;</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒈</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">&gt;</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|f(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1})-f(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0})-&lt;\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}),\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle-&lt;\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}),\boldsymbol{\xi}^{*}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}&gt;\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">&lt;</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒈</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-&lt;\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}),\boldsymbol{\xi}^{*}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}&gt;\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\overline{C}_{1}w^{-1/6}\sqrt{\log w}t^{2/3}\lambda^{-2/3}L^{3}+\|&lt;\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}),\boldsymbol{\xi}^{*}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}&gt;\|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathsize="0.900em">C</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></msub><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">6</mn></mrow></msup><msqrt><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi></mrow></msqrt><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">L</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">3</mn></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" mathsize="0.900em">&lt;</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒈</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overline{C}_{1}w^{-1/6}\sqrt{\log w}t^{2/3}\lambda^{-2/3}L^{3}+\|&lt;\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}),\boldsymbol{\xi}^{*}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}&gt;\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">where the first equality holds due to <math id="Sx1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> by the random initialization of <math id="Sx1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the inequality
holds due to Lemma 4.1 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">53</a>]</cite> with the fact <math id="Sx1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}\|_{2}\leq 2\sqrt{t/(w\lambda)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><mrow><mn mathsize="0.900em">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">λ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}\|_{2}\leq 2\sqrt{t/(w\lambda)}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the second term, we have the following bound:</p>
</div>
<div id="Sx1.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="Sx1.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Sx1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.E12.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\|&lt;\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}),\boldsymbol{\xi}^{*}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}&gt;\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" mathsize="0.900em">&lt;</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒈</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|&lt;\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0}),\boldsymbol{\xi}^{*}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}&gt;\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="0.900em">≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\|&lt;\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}),\boldsymbol{\xi}^{*}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}&gt;\|+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" mathsize="0.900em">&lt;</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒈</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">+</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|&lt;\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}),\boldsymbol{\xi}^{*}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}&gt;\|+</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Sx1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Sx1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\|&lt;\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0})-\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}),\boldsymbol{\xi}^{*}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}&gt;\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" mathsize="0.900em">&lt;</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒈</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mn mathsize="0.900em">0</mn></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒈</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝒙</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><msub><mi mathsize="0.900em">𝝃</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">t</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">−</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">1</mn></mrow></msub><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">&gt;</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|&lt;\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{0})-\boldsymbol{g}(\boldsymbol{x},\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}),\boldsymbol{\xi}^{*}-\boldsymbol{\xi}_{t-1}&gt;\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
